Author: Rodrigo Aurelio Criscuolo
Date: 10/07/2026
Topic: Device Identity, Registration, and Management
Scope: Microsoft Intune + Microsoft Entra ID
Purpose: Provide a complete, structured, cloud‑ready knowledge base for device identity, enrollment, management, troubleshooting, and architecture.

1. Identity vs. Management (Entra ID vs. Intune)
  - Core concept
  Understanding the difference between device identity (Microsoft Entra ID) and device management (Microsoft Intune) is the foundation of all modern endpoint architecture.

    A useful distinction first.
  Microsoft Intune: enrollment connects the device to Intune for management.
  Microsoft Entra registration: join creates a cloud identity for the device.
  Note, its importante, a device can have an Entra identity withou being managed by Intune. Intune enrollmente install an MDM certificate so Intune can apply policies and manage it.
  Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/device-enrollment/guide

1.1 Device Identity (Microsoft Entra ID)
  Entra ID provides cloud identity for devices through:
    Registration (BYOD)
    Join (Corporate)
    Hybrid Join (AD + Entra)
  Identity enables:
    Conditional Access
    SSO
    Device-based authentication
    Compliance evaluation

But identity alone does not manage the device.

1.2 Device Management (Microsoft Intune)
  Intune provides:
    Configuration profiles
    Compliance policies
    App deployment
    Security baselines
    Remote actions (wipe, retire, lock)

Management requires MDM enrollment, which installs an MDM certificate.
A device can have an Entra ID identity without being Intune-managed. This is the most common misunderstanding.

2. Device Identity Types
  There are three identity states in MS Entra ID:

Personal/BYOD device       → Entra registered ── (optional) ──→ Intune-managed
New corporate cloud device → Entra joined ─────── (usually) ──→ Intune-managed
Existing AD-domain device  → Hybrid joined ────── (often) ────→ Intune-managed

2.1 Comparison. How the three identity types differ

Identity type       | What the device is connected to                | Typical example                            | How the user signs into Windows             | Usual management
                    |                                                |                                            |                                             |
MS Entra Registered | Entra ID: The device remains independently     | Employee adds a work account to a personal | Personal account: work account is added for | Often app Protection or limited management,
                    | owned or configured                            | Windows PC                                 | organizational access                       | can also enroll in Intune
                    |                                                |                                            |                                             |
MS Entra Joined     | Entra ID only: no on-premises AD domain join   | New company laptop set up from home        | Work or school account                      | Intune is a common choice
                    |                                                |                                            |                                             |
MS Entra Hybrid     | Both on-premises Active Directory and Entra ID | Existing domain-joined company PC          | On-premises domain account                  | Group Policy, Configuration Manager, Intune, 
                    |                                                |                                            |                                             | or co-management

Note: 
Registered is generally the BYOD/ work-account case:adding a work account gives the device a cloud identity, but does not by itself turn it into an Entra-Joined corporate PC.
Joined is a cloud-first corporate device
Hybrid joined is both, keeps the on-premises domain relationship as well as the cloud identity. Hybrid devices may need periodic connectivity to on-primises domain controllers.

Sources: 
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/devices/concept-hybrid-join
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/devices/concept-directory-join

3. Identity Types

  3.1 Entra Registered (BYOD)
    Personal device
    Work account added
    Cloud identity created
    Device remains personal
  Management optional
  Best for App Protection (MAM)

  3.2 Entra Joined (Cloud-first Corporate)
    Corporate-owned
    Cloud-native
    Autopilot recommended
    Intune automatic enrollment
    No dependency on AD

  3.3 Hybrid Joined (AD + Entra)
    Domain-joined
    Syncs to Entra
    Requires DC connectivity
    Supports legacy apps
    Supports co-management

4. Flow Decision (Mermaid)
    A [Start: What type of device is it?] --> B{Is it a device corporated?}

    B -->|Yes| C{Is it new or existing?}
    B -->|No (Personal/BYOD)| D[Entra Registered]

    C -->|New device| E[Entra Joined]
    C -->|Existing AD device| F[Hybrid Joined]

    D --> G{Management Needed?}
    G -->|App-level only| H[Use App Protection (MAM)]
    G -->|Full device control| I[Intune Enrollment (BYOD Policy Required)]

    E --> J[Intune Automatic Enrollment (Autopilot Recommended)]

    F --> K[Intune Enrollment via GPO]
    F --> L[Co-management with ConfigMgr]

    H --> M[End]

5. Recommended Join + Enrollment Patterns

  5.1 New Corporate Devices
    Entra Join + Intune automatic enrollment
    Prefer Windows Autopilot
    Cloud-first, simplest configuration
    Reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/device-enrollment/enroll-devices

  5.2 Existing AD Domain Devices
    Hybrid Join + Intune enrollment via GPO
    Required for AD-based apps, GPO, machine auth
    Needs periodic DC connectivity
    Reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/devices/concept-hybrid-join

  5.3 Personal / BYOD Devices
    Choose between App Protection (MAM) or full MDM
    Entra registration ≠ Intune enrollment
    Full MDM gives the org device control → must match BYOD policy
    Reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/device-enrollment/enroll-devices

