  6.4 Error: Autopilot device not joining Entra
    Fix: Check profile assignment + MDM scope + hash upload.
  ... in progress...

  6.5 Error: Corporate devices show as Registered
    Fix: Re-provision via Autopilot or Entra Join.
  ... in progress...


Important
The most common source of trouble is choosing a join method that doesn't fit the device, or assuming that a device's Entra record proves it is Intune managed.

For each device class
  * For New Corporate device, prefer Microsoft Entra Join + Intune automatic enrollment, ideally through Windows Autopilot for repeatable provisioning.
    Microsoft describes Entra Join as easier to configure than hybrid join for new deployments. 
    Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/device-enrollment/enroll-devices

  * For Existing AD-domain device: Use Hybrid Join + Intune enrollment, usually triggered by Group Policy. This is appropriate where you still need AD domain services, Group Policy, or apps that rely on AD machine authentication. hybrid Joined Devices periodically needs line of sight to domain controles.
    Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/devices/concept-hybrid-join
            https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/device-enrollment/enroll-devices

  * For Personal/ BYOD device: Choose deliberately between app-level protection and or full device management.
    Entra registration alone is not Intune enrollment. If you enroll a personal device in Intune, you're giving the organization device management capabilities, ensure that matches your BYOD policy and user expectations.
    Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/device-enrollment/enroll-devices

Entra registration would not be used as workaround to manage a fleet of corporate, domain-joined devices, and we would not use the hybrid join GPO method for registered/ BYOD devices. The supported GPO auto-enrollmente scenario is for eligible hydrid joined devices.
Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/device-enrollment/enroll-devices
        https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/answers/questions/2203129/issues-with-device-enrollment-in-intune


